# check: fail error[O38]: this argument borrows an own object, and the callee may keep it beyond the call
# vec1 review, found beside it: a conversion names its argument's storage (T29a), so "String(v.View())" keeps the view's
# loan - pushed into a List of text it would outlive the buffer the next Push replaces
fn main() ? {
    v := Vec<Char>()
    v.Push('a')
    l := List<String&>()
    l.Push(String(v.View()))
    for i in range 100 { v.Push('b') }
    println(l[0])
}
